---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Qingdao Walking Tour — Old Town Self-Guided Walk" description="Self-guided walking tour through Qingdao Old Town. Zhanqiao Pier to Badaguan, 5km, 2-3 hours. Route map, photo stops, food stops, and local tips." pageType="Article">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="tag mb-3">Route</p>
      <h1 class="mb-2">Qingdao Old Town Walking Tour</h1>
      <p class="body-lg mb-10 max-w-[65ch]">A 5km self-guided walk from Zhanqiao Pier to Badaguan, through the heart of Qingdao's Old Town. Cobblestones, German villas, church spires, seafood streets, and sea views — all at a relaxed pace.</p>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-10">
        <div class="card p-5 text-center"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1">Distance</h4><p class="caption">5 km (3.1 miles)</p></div>
        <div class="card p-5 text-center"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1">Duration</h4><p class="caption">2–3 hours at a relaxed pace</p></div>
        <div class="card p-5 text-center"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1">Difficulty</h4><p class="tag">Easy — flat</p></div>
        <div class="card p-5 text-center"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1">Best Time</h4><p class="caption">Morning (8–11am) or late afternoon</p></div>
      </div>

      <!-- Route overview -->
      <div class="card p-6 mb-10 bg-[var(--color-accent-subtle)]/30">
        <h2 class="h3 mb-3">Route Overview</h2>
        <p class="caption">Zhanqiao Pier → Zhongshan Road → St. Michael's Cathedral → Lao She's Residence → Observatory → No. 1 Bathing Beach → Badaguan. Mostly flat with one short uphill climb to the observatory (5 min). Comfortable walking shoes recommended. The entire route is in Shinan District and well-signed.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Route Stops -->
      <h2 class="h3 mb-6">Route Stops — Step by Step</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 mb-10">
        <!-- Stop 1 -->
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">1</div>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Zhanqiao Pier — Start Here</h4>
              <p class="caption leading-relaxed">Qingdao's most famous landmark. Walk the 440m pier to the octagonal pavilion at the end. Morning light is best for photos looking back at the city skyline. The pier was built in 1891 and has been rebuilt several times. Free entry, open 24/7.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Photo tip:</strong> Stand at the pier tip facing west for the classic skyline shot with the pier as a leading line. Go before 9am to avoid crowds.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-1 text-[var(--color-accent)]">⏱ Spend: 30–45 min</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Stop 2 -->
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">2</div>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Zhongshan Road & St. Michael's Cathedral</h4>
              <p class="caption leading-relaxed">Walk 10 min northwest from the pier along tree-lined streets. Zhongshan Road is Qingdao's historic shopping street, lined with converted German buildings now housing cafes and boutiques. St. Michael's Cathedral dominates the skyline with its twin 56m Neo-Romanesque spires, built by German missionaries in 1934.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Entry:</strong> ¥10 for the cathedral. Open 08:00–17:00. The interior has stunning stained glass and vaulted ceilings. Sunday mass at 10am is atmospheric but busy.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-1"><strong>Food stop:</strong> Just behind the cathedral, walk down to Pichai Yuan (劈柴院) — a historic food alley since 1902. Try grilled squid and Qingdao potstickers (guotie). Budget: ¥20–40.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-1 text-[var(--color-accent)]">⏱ Spend: 45–60 min (including Pichai Yuan snack)</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Stop 3 -->
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">3</div>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Lao She's Former Residence</h4>
              <p class="caption leading-relaxed">8 min walk southwest from the cathedral. The famous Chinese novelist Lao She (老舍) lived here in the 1930s and wrote parts of his masterpiece "Rickshaw Boy" (骆驼祥子) in this house. Small museum with original furniture, manuscripts, and photos. Free entry.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Address:</strong> 5 Huangxian Road (黄县路5号). Look for the bronze statue of Lao She in the garden.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-1 text-[var(--color-accent)]">⏱ Spend: 20–30 min</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Stop 4 -->
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">4</div>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Qingdao Observatory — The Viewpoint</h4>
              <p class="caption leading-relaxed">10 min walk uphill from Lao She's house. Built in 1898 on Guanxiang Hill (观象山, 79m). The best panoramic view of Old Town red-tiled roofs against the sea. The hilltop park is quiet and shaded — a perfect rest stop.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Entry:</strong> ¥15. Open 08:00–18:00.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Warning:</strong> This is the only uphill section (about 5 min of climbing). Take it slow. The view from the top is worth every step.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-1 text-[var(--color-accent)]">⏱ Spend: 20–30 min</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Stop 5 -->
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">5</div>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">No. 1 Bathing Beach</h4>
              <p class="caption leading-relaxed">5 min downhill from the observatory. Qingdao's oldest and most central beach. A crescent of sand tucked between the Old Town and the sea. Busy in summer but beautiful at sunset. The water is cleanest in June–September.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Swimming:</strong> Safe between the flags. Lifeguards on duty June–September. Water temperature: 18–25°C in summer.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Rest stop:</strong> There is a small cafe at the east end. Or walk 5 min east to the Badaguan area for more options.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-1 text-[var(--color-accent)]">⏱ Spend: 20–30 min (longer if swimming)</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Stop 6 -->
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm">6</div>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h4 class="font-semibold mb-2">Badaguan Scenic Area — The Finale</h4>
              <p class="caption leading-relaxed">10 min east along the coast from No. 1 Beach. The crown jewel of the walk. Tree-lined streets named after ancient Chinese military passes, with over 200 German-era villas in Gothic, Baroque, and Rococo styles. The famous "Princess House" (公主楼) is a fairytale-like Danish-style villa painted green.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Best seasons:</strong> Cherry blossom in April, golden ginkgo leaves in October–November. Both are magical.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Free to wander.</strong> The Princess House costs ¥15 to enter. Allow 1–2 hours to explore all the streets properly.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-1"><strong>End here:</strong> Badaguan connects to the seaside promenade. Continue east to May Fourth Square (30 min walk) or grab a coffee at one of the Badaguan cafes.</p>
              <p class="caption mt-1 text-[var(--color-accent)]">⏱ Spend: 1–2 hours</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Practical info -->
      <h2 class="h3 mb-4">Practical Information</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-10">
        <div class="card p-5">
          <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-2">What to Bring</h4>
          <ul class="caption space-y-1">
            <li>Comfortable walking shoes (cobblestones are uneven)</li>
            <li>Water bottle — refill at hotels or convenience stores</li>
            <li>Sunscreen and hat (summer) or warm layers (winter)</li>
            <li>Camera — every corner is photogenic</li>
            <li>Small cash for street food and small attractions</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-5">
          <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-2">Getting to the Start / End</h4>
          <ul class="caption space-y-1">
            <li><strong>Start (Zhanqiao):</strong> Metro Line 3 to Qingdao Station, 10 min walk. Or any bus to Zhongshan Road.</li>
            <li><strong>End (Badaguan):</strong> Metro Line 3 to Huiquan Square. Or walk 30 min more to May Fourth Square.</li>
            <li><strong>Return:</strong> Metro Line 3 runs the full route back. Or Didi to your hotel (¥10–20).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex gap-4">
        <a href="/qingdao-routes/cycling" class="btn-outline">Cycling Route</a>
        <a href="/qingdao-itineraries/2-days" class="btn-ghost">2-Day Itinerary</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
